Negative control for the refused group's ring standoff being reserved on EVERY
side (`H6` · `AC6.1` · `AC6.4`).

Takes the standoff back to the horizontal axis alone. Every structural claim
survives — the ring is still the ui vocabulary, still on the `<tbody>` that
holds the row AND its reason, still with no fill — so the mark looks correct in
the middle of a long list. It is the record at the BOTTOM that loses: the ui
`Table` draws its own `overflow-auto` scroller, and with no vertical padding the
last group's outline is clipped where it should close, which is the ring reading
as landing on the wrong row.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the row-ring spec — the table no longer reserves the offset plus the
outline's width on the axis the scroller clips, so the standoff case fails while
the enclosure, vocabulary and no-fill cases stay green.

